to: planner
reason: plan-accuracy — §14.1 F2 "cheap half" premise is infeasible for the fixture it names
refs:
  - planning/ta-anchor-refactor-v2-plan.md (§14.1 F2)
  - planning/ta-anchor-refactor-v2-code-review.md (F2 section)
  - ta-anchor-refactor-v2/internal/engines/saturation/engine.go:1795-1798, 1594-1596
  - ta-anchor-refactor-v2/internal/engines/saturation/engine_test.go (Test 5, ~:248)
  - ta-anchor-refactor-v2/internal/metrics/metrics.go:45
note: |
  Finding for the plan's awareness (coder investigation, 2026-08-06). Dean has already
  decided the disposition; this is so §14.1 F2 can be corrected to match the code.

  §14.1 F2 (and the review doc's F2) recommend a "cheap half": add a
  Status.DesiredOptimizedAlloc.NumReplicas-unchanged assertion to Test 5 "via a k8s-client
  read of the VA." That premise does not hold for Test 5's fixture:

  - Test 5 lives in the "When handling multiple VariantAutoscalings" Context, whose
    BeforeEach creates Deployments + annotated HPAs only — NO VariantAutoscaling CRs. The
    variants are annotation-sourced (synthesized in-memory from the HPAs).
  - For annotation-sourced variants the engine persists NO CRD status. engine.go:1795-1798:
    "KEDA/HPA reads wva_desired_replicas directly. There is no CRD status to patch, so no
    cache write or reconcile trigger is needed." applySaturationDecisions operates on an
    in-memory *va.DeepCopy() (engine.go:1594-1596) and never writes it back to the API server.
  - So there is no VA object to read after optimize(); a k8s-client VA-status read returns
    nothing. The only held-replica observable is the wva_desired_replicas gauge
    (internal/metrics/metrics.go:45 — package-private `desiredReplicas *prometheus.GaugeVec`),
    which is exactly the fragile, parallel-Ginkgo-racy half the coder had already flagged.

  Net: for this fixture the "cheap half" and the "fragile metric half" collapse into one
  fragile observable — the cheap, non-flaky k8s-read assertion the review envisioned does
  not exist here. (It WOULD exist for a model-sourced / CRD-persisted fixture, which is
  likely where the recommendation came from.)

  Dean's decision (2026-08-06): F2 is knowingly relaxed for the annotation-sourced fixture —
  keep the existing distributed coverage (Test 4B no-decision + no-panic; the pre-existing
  applySaturationDecisions hold tests; Test 5's optimize()-nil + empty QueryCallCounts +
  logged-refusal), and record the relaxation of plan Test 4's "assert replicas unchanged +
  metric emitted" clause in the push-ready sync handoff. Dean's explicit sign-off is on record
  (coder status file, Post-review findings). No code change.

  Suggested §14.1 F2 correction (planner's call): note that the cheap-half k8s-read assertion
  is infeasible for the annotation-sourced Test 5 fixture (engine persists no CRD status;
  engine.go:1795-1798), that both halves collapse into the package-private gauge, and that
  Dean signed off on keeping the distributed coverage. F1's disposition (ride the post-#1513
  rebase) is unchanged and needs no plan edit.
